        "text": "Smart contracts are a crucial element for DEFI products to function. So what exactly are smart contracts? Let's start with a brief history of the concept behind them. Lawyer and computer scientist Nick Szabo first described the idea of smart contracts in the 1990s. A smart contract is a tool that formalizes and secures computer networks by combining protocols with user interfaces. Potential uses were envisioned in fields involving contractual agreements, such as credit systems and content rights management, but it was only after the launch of the ethereum network in 2015 that smart contracts gained wider adoption in the world of cryptocurrencies. A smart contract refers to self executing computer programs that run on the blockchain when predetermined conditions are met. The conditions are predefined by computer code, which is replicated and executed by all network nodes.",
